  {
    "id": "event-6mla8ij1re9i1jdpf7a11b8s2c@google.com",
    "category": "events",
    "timestamp": "2016-09-14T01:00:00.000Z",
    "title": "[Revelation] Just realized I solved my career",
    "detail": {
      "calendar": "Revelation",
      "summary": "Just realized I solved my career",
      "description": "<html-blob>Test the ethics of religion in the workplace by measuring productivity output in JIRA:<br><br>I am all knowing.  I am science.  I am father time and I will prove it to you (responsibility).  I am your successor (family/faith).  I am comedy (happiness/emotion).  I am ahead of my time (confidence).  I can afford to wait for opportunity (ambition).  I will hold you accountable to the truth and I need you to hold me accountable (trust/responsibility).  Mindset IS everything and I can hack yours.  Prove to me you are more successful, and I will realize my own ambitions.  Love and trust everyone and that will save us all some time and work.  Stop worrying about consequences because we already know how this ends. Communicate with people around you, and you will notice there is no such thing as coincidence, only opportunities.  Human ambition is limitless so you should stress people to work harder for you and they will help you save time talking about it.<br><br><br>I need everyone's help on this.<br>Practice makes perfect!<br>1) Brainstorm, read new news, seek out new sources of information, youtube new topics that don't even interest you, do research into things that are beautiful, criticize everything with a skeptical mind, and recognize good from the bad so that you may focus on the good, joyful<br>2) Enjoy the outdoors, get fresh air, work outside, do something with water, swim, fly, drink, do something in the snow, cardiovascular exercise, hiking, running<br>3) Do something with your hands, down and dirty, garden, rock climb, plant a tree, dig something up, build something<br>Encourage people to sign up for safeway delivery by next wednesday, then try next thursday and record how many people sign up on each day<br>4) Listening to parents and studying history helps us understand how things got to where they are today.  Parents teach us right from wrong, even by example of doing right and wrong.  Create, time management, focus on challenges, listen to the people smarter than you and to what they say, history and past experience have the right answers not you, connect with someone much older than you, visit your grandmother, compare your life and how you live to theirs and question if it is wrong or right, take care of a child, set a good example for someone<br>5) Do something kind for someone else, why else would everyone love FRIDAY!  Meet with old and new friends, play with your pets, feed birds at a duck pond, smile and make eye contact with someone you don't know, appreciate the people around you, \"people watch\"<br>6) We are all in this together.  Share this list with everyone you know and help them understand and practice it, think about what you can do to improve yourself and be more tolerant, help a homeless person, do community service, pick up trash somewhere (from the night before? :P )  catch up on everything you tried to get done during the week because you were too busy being your perfect self, eat plants only (be vegetarian for 1 day a week) (is this possible remedy to hangover?)  clean up your backyard, clean your house, clean everything<br>7) Rest, sleep, meditate, don't do anything on the computer, yoga, this could be the only day you need to sleep with proper exercise, think about being immortal<br><br><br><br>I know something that you don't know that I know.<br>I know that you know that and I know that too.<br><br>Coincidence Calendar switched to this tab as soon as I was ready to paste something?</html-blob>",
      "location": "",
      "start": "2016-09-14T01:00:00.000Z",
      "end": "2016-09-14T02:00:00.000Z",
      "isPublic": true
    }
  },
